# Copy to .env.local for `npm run dev`. Never commit real values.

# The web app connects as pharmacy_app: not a superuser, no BYPASSRLS, owns nothing (06a §2.2).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://pharmacy_app:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/pharmacy

# The migration runner connects as pharmacy_migrator, the only role that owns tables (06a §18).
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://pharmacy_migrator:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/pharmacy

# Optional: how long a passed schema self-check is trusted, in ms (default 30000).
# SELF_CHECK_TTL_MS=30000

# Signs the session cookie (HS256). At least 32 random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Changing it signs everyone out.
SESSION_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_TO_32_OR_MORE_RANDOM_CHARACTERS

# The PIN pepper (06a §3.12): comma-separated v<n>:<base64 of 32+ random bytes>; the highest
# version is current. Never in the database, logs or the repo. `npm start` refuses to start
# without a valid one. Generate: echo "v1:$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
PIN_PEPPERS=CHANGE_ME

# The founder CLI (scripts/create-org.ts) connects as pharmacy_ops. Not used by the web app.
# OPS_DATABASE_URL=postgres://pharmacy_ops:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/pharmacy

# Optional: mark the session cookie Secure outside production (production always does).
# COOKIE_SECURE=1

# The medicine-master loader (scripts/load-master.cjs) connects as pharmacy_curator. Not used by the web app.
# CURATOR_DATABASE_URL=postgres://pharmacy_curator:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/pharmacy

# Optional: the desk ⇄ pharmacy stock sync (D-57, 06a §12.5). Off unless all three are set; off,
# every /api/integrations/desk/** route answers 404. The key is shared with the desk's server
# (at least 32 random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`); the organisation and premises are
# where the desk's bills take stock (never taken from a request).
# DESK_SYNC_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# DESK_SYNC_ORG_SLUG=my-clinic
# DESK_SYNC_PREMISES_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# D-64: the clinic's own password for deleting a medicine, as a scrypt hash (lib/auth/password.ts hashPassword). Unset: Delete asks for the login password.
# ITEM_DELETE_PASSWORD_HASH=
